{"event_type":"review","id":"6b77aba70ef0438d89632133d114f589cf9eb8392dc86819c8a089e4aedfd496","occurred_at":"2026-11-02T04:28:26Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5b95d12344d49c51ee705c333e8241af90e96808055b8b35476ff01b8a1e165b","sha256":"5b95d12344d49c51ee705c333e8241af90e96808055b8b35476ff01b8a1e165b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4390566d41f60abc5ab7350ee24c3a925cccc1ebc5292b4e2b4ab7a86121d263","sha256":"4390566d41f60abc5ab7350ee24c3a925cccc1ebc5292b4e2b4ab7a86121d263"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c5c4cf2c235ec5ccd35cb9f67bcce86382ad3625f7a35d8989493bd6f96d3262","sha256":"c5c4cf2c235ec5ccd35cb9f67bcce86382ad3625f7a35d8989493bd6f96d3262"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f830223dd29dc2db51b094d3a6ee4fc4d7cf1ea29e0608abbcb3f16f408d8289","sha256":"f830223dd29dc2db51b094d3a6ee4fc4d7cf1ea29e0608abbcb3f16f408d8289"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1a548ccd4b54d7e9a57bc848f48dd6bb105cd49548048b9a90d6c7366b18cc3b","sha256":"1a548ccd4b54d7e9a57bc848f48dd6bb105cd49548048b9a90d6c7366b18cc3b"}],"attempt_id":"5177abdf7b2b63166e1e968e497efbab377c462aa6f8ac2e14e6ee7dfe9c4a45:0:1","base":"f820e9ddaea1b589e327b862c8523e7e42297449","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"d7f1399f669b68c26b18b535ae5903350335ca54","body":"**Map a receipt integrity failure to `failed`, not `needs-human`.**\n\nLines 100-104 report a receipt that differs from the verified bytes as `status: 'failed'`. `readQueueEvidence` throws instead for a digest mismatch or a schema parse failure. These throws reach `guardDevOp`, which returns `needs-human` with \"environment read or execution failed\". A tampered or corrupt receipt therefore gets a different status from the deep-equality mismatch a few lines later.\n\nCatch the `readQueueEvidence` throw here. Return `failed` with `faultText(err)`. A missing file (ENOENT) can still escape to the guard as an environment fault if you want that split.\n\nAs per path instructions: \"a public op maps failure onto the frozen taxonomy (status 'failed' with error), never a fabricated ok.\"\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      const evidence = await readQueueEvidence(\n-        join(root, '.cq', 'queue-evidence'),\n-        imported.debt.completion.receiptId,\n-      );\n+      let evidence;\n+      try {\n+        evidence = await readQueueEvidence(\n+          join(root, '.cq', 'queue-evidence'),\n+          imported.debt.completion.receiptId,\n+        );\n+      } catch (err) {\n+        return {\n+          status: 'failed',\n+          error: `dev.disposition: imported receipt failed verification — ${faultText(err)}`,\n+        };\n+      }\n```\n</details>","id":"e968a573cc3075a610f332a29a72d1a4783df5bcd928a5af8dcc6e3451264367","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/disposition.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Map a receipt integrity failure to `failed`, not `needs-human`."}],"head":"aa5b3631d44a57531e942b1c838d4979dd220e89","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"d5fc53e567171872007ef8c6899a11ea12691730","intervals":[[1,2594]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_crq.py"},{"blob":"157aa6f8d00c09737eb39baa4e21e276124c6894","intervals":[[1,376]],"path":"src/ops/dev/coderabbit.ts"},{"blob":"d7f1399f669b68c26b18b535ae5903350335ca54","intervals":[[1,133]],"path":"src/ops/dev/disposition.ts"}],"job_id":"5177abdf7b2b63166e1e968e497efbab377c462aa6f8ac2e14e6ee7dfe9c4a45:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"d5fc53e567171872007ef8c6899a11ea12691730","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_crq.py","reason"